{
  "title": "24: al-Noor النور",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nسُوْرَةٌ اَنْزَلْنٰهَا وَفَرَضْنٰهَا وَاَنْزَلْنَا فِيْهَاۤ اٰيٰتٍۭ بَيِّنٰتٍ لَّعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(1)\nSOORATUN AANZALNAAHAA WAFARAZNAAHAA WA ANZALNAA FEEHAA AAYAATIM BAYYENAAT LA-A’LLAKUM TAZAKKAROON.\n(This) ‘Surah’ which We have sent down, and which We have ordained; and We have sent down therein clear signs, that ye may take heed.\nاَلزَّانِيَةُ وَالزَّانِىْ فَاجْلِدُوْا كُلَّ وَاحِدٍ مِّنْهُمَا مِائَةَ جَلْدَةٍ‌وَّلَا تَاْخُذْكُمْ بِهِمَا رَاْفَةٌ فِىْ دِيْنِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ‌ۚ وَلْيَشْهَدْ عَذَابَهُمَا طَآئِفَةٌ مِّنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(2)\nAALZZAANEETU WAALZZAANEAA FAAJLEDOOA KULLA WAAHEDIN MINHOMAA WA A’AMIN JALDATINWWALAA TAAKHUZKUM BEHEMAA RAAFATUN FEE DEEN LAAHE IN KUNTUM TUMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE WALYASHHAD A’AZAABAHUMAA TAAEFATUN MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nThe fornicatress and fornicator scourge ye each of them (with) a hundred stripes, and let not pity for them keep you away from enforcing the sentence of God, if ye believe in God and the Last Day; and let their chastisement be witnessed by a party of the believers.\nاَلزَّانِىْ لَا يَنْكِحُ اِلَّا زَانِيَةً اَوْ مُشْرِكَةً  وَّ الزَّانِيَةُ لَا يَنْكِحُهَاۤ اِلَّا زَانٍ اَوْ مُشْرِكٌ‌ ۚ وَحُرِّمَ ذٰ لِكَ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(3)\nAALZZAANEAA LAA YANKEHU ILLAA ZAANEETAN AW MUSHREKATAN WA AZ-ZAANEETU LAA YANKEHUHAA ILLAA ZAANIN AW MUSHREKUN WAHURREMA ZAA LEKA A’LAL MOAMENEEN.\nThe fornicator marrieth not but a fornicatress or an idolatress, and the fornicatress marrieth not but a fornicator or an idolator; and it is forbidden unto the believers.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَرْمُوْنَ الْمُحْصَنٰتِ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَاْتُوْا بِاَرْبَعَةِ شُهَدَآءَ فَاجْلِدُوْهُمْ ثَمٰنِيْنَ جَلْدَةً وَّلَا تَقْبَلُوْا لَهُمْ شَهَادَةً اَبَدًا‌ ۚ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْفٰسِقُوْنَ ۙ‏(4)\nWAL LAZEENA YARMOONA AL-MUHSANAATE SUMMA LAM YAATOOA BE-AR-BA-A’TE SHOHADAAA-A FAAJLEDOOHUM SAMAANEENA JALDATAN WA LAA TAQBALOOA LAHUM SHA-HAADATAN ABADAM WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL FAASEQOON.\nAnd those who accuse protected women (with adultery) (and) then bring not four witnesses (supporting the charge), scourge them (with) fourscore stripes, and (after that) accept ye not their testimony for ever; and these it is the wicked (ones),\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰلِكَ وَاَصْلَحُوْا‌ۚ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(5)\nILLAA LAZEENA TAABOO MIN BA’DE ZAALEKA WA ASLAHOO FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nSave those who repent after this and amend themselves, for verily God is Oft-Forgiving All- Merciful.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يَرْمُوْنَ اَزْوَاجَهُمْ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَّهُمْ شُهَدَآءُ اِلَّاۤ اَنْفُسُهُمْ فَشَهَادَةُ اَحَدِهِمْ اَرْبَعُ شَهٰدٰتٍۭ بِاللّٰهِ‌ۙ اِنَّهٗ لَمِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(6)\nWAL LAZEENA YARMOONA AAZWAAJAHUM WA LAM YAKUL LAHUM SHUHADAAU ILLAA ANFOSOHUM FASHAHAADATU AAHADEHEM AARBAU’U SHAHAADAATIN BIL-LAAHE INNAHU LAMENAS SAADEQEENA.\nFor those who accuse their wives while they have no witnesses save themselves, then the testimony of one of them (shall be taken) four times (swearing) by God that verily he is of the truthful (ones)\nوَالْخَامِسَةُ اَنَّ لَعْنَتَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِ اِنْ كَانَ مِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(7)\nWAL KHAAMESATU ANNAL LAA’NATA LAAHE A’LAYHE IN KAANA MENAL KAAZEBEEN.\nAnd the fifth (oath to be) that the curse of God on him if he be one of the liars.\nوَيَدْرَؤُا عَنْهَا الْعَذَابَ اَنْ تَشْهَدَ اَرْبَعَ شَهٰدٰتٍۢ بِاللّٰهِ‌ۙ اِنَّهٗ لَمِنَ الْكٰذِبِيْنَۙ‏(8)\nWAYADRAUA A’NHAA A’ZAABA AN TASHHADA AARBAA’A SHAHAADAATIN BIL-LAAHE INNAHU LAMENAS KAAZEBEEN.\nAnd it shall avert the punishment from her if she testify four times (swearing) by God, that verily he is one of liars,\nوَالْخَامِسَةَ اَنَّ غَضَبَ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهَاۤ اِنْ كَانَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(9)\nWAL KHAAMESATA ANNAL GHAZABA LAAHE A’LAYHAA IN KAANA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\nAnd the fifth (path) to be that the wrath of God be on her if he be of the truthful ones\nوَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهٗ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ تَوَّابٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(10)\nWA LAWLAA FAZLUL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA RAHMATOHU WA ANNAL LAAHA TAWABUN HAKEEM.\nAnd had it not been God’s grace upon you and His mercy - and that God is Oft-Returning, All-Wise (ye had been ruined indeed).\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ جَآءُوْ بِالْاِفْكِ عُصْبَةٌ مِّنْكُمْ‌ ؕ لَا تَحْسَبُوْهُ شَرًّا لَّكُمْ‌ ؕ بَلْ هُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ‌ ؕ لِكُلِّ امْرِىٴٍ مِّنْهُمْ مَّا اكْتَسَبَ مِنَ الْاِثْمِ‌ ۚ وَالَّذِىْ تَوَلّٰى كِبْرَهٗ مِنْهُمْ لَهٗ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(11)\nINNAL LAZEENA JAAA-OO BIL-AEFKE U’USBATUN MINKUM LAA TAHSABOOHU SHARRAN-Y LAKUM BAL HOWA KHAYRUL LAKUM LEKULLIM AMREAA MINHUM MAA AKTASABA MENAL AL-AESME WAL LAZEE TAWALLAA KEBRAH MINHUM LAHU A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nVerily those who have brought forth the slander are a gang among you, deem it not an evil unto you; Nay! It is good for you. Unto every man of them (shall come the punishment for) what he hath earned of the sin; and for him of them who took the greater part therein shall be a grievous chastisement.\nلَوْلَاۤ اِذْ سَمِعْتُمُوْهُ ظَنَّ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنٰتُ بِاَنْفُسِهِمْ خَيْرًاۙ وَّقَالُوْا هٰذَاۤ اِفْكٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(12)\nLAWLAA IZ SAMEA’TUMOOHU ZANNAS MOAMENOONA WAL MUMENAATU BE-ANFOSEHIM KHAYRAN WA QAALOO HAAZAA AEFKUN MOBEEN.\nWhy did not the believer men and the believer women when ye heard of it, think well of themselves, and say: “This is a clear slander\nلَوْلَا جَآءُوْ عَلَيْهِ بِاَرْبَعَةِ شُهَدَآءَ‌ ۚ فَاِذْ لَمْ يَاْتُوْا بِالشُّهَدَآءِ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ هُمُ الْكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(13)\nLAWLAA JAAA-OO A’LAYHE BE-AR-BA-A’TE SHOHADAAA-A FA IZ LAM YAATOOA BE-AN FA-OOLAAA-EKA I’NDAL LAAHE HOMUL AL-KAAZEBOONA.\nWhy did they not produce four witnesses about it? But since they did not produce any witnesses, with God they are the liars.\nوَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهٗ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ لَمَسَّكُمْ فِىْ مَاۤ اَفَضْتُمْ فِيْهِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌ‌ ۖ‌ ۚ‏(14)\nWA LAWLAA FAZLUL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA RAHMATOHU FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH LAMASSAKUM FEE MAA AFAZTUM FEEHE A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nAnd had it not been God’s grace upon you and His mercy in this world and the hereafter, indeed had seized you for the slander ye entered into, a grievous chastisement.\nاِذْ تَلَقَّوْنَهٗ بِاَ لْسِنَتِكُمْ وَتَقُوْلُوْنَ بِاَ فْوَاهِكُمْ مَّا لَيْسَ لَكُمْ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ وَّتَحْسَبُوْنَهٗ هَيِّنًا ‌ ۖ  وَّهُوَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ عَظِيْمٌ‏(15)\nIZ TALAQQAWNAH BE-AFWAAHEKUM LSENATEKUM WA TAQOOLOONA BE-AFWAAHEKUM WAL MAA LAYSA LAKUM BEHI I’LMUM WWATAHSABOONAH HAYNAN WA I’NDAL LAAHE A’ZEEM.\nWhen ye received it with your tongues and uttered it with your mouths what ye had no knowledge of, and ye deemed it a light matter; while with God it was grievous.\nوَ لَوْلَاۤ اِذْ سَمِعْتُمُوْهُ قُلْتُمْ مَّا يَكُوْنُ لَنَاۤ اَنْ نَّتَكَلَّمَ بِهٰذَ ا ‌ۖ  سُبْحٰنَكَ هٰذَا بُهْتَانٌ عَظِيْمٌ‏(16)\nWA LAWLAA IZ SAMEA’TUMOOHU IZ QULTUM MAA LAHUL LANAA AN NNATAKALLAMA BEHAAZA A SUBHAANAKA HAAZAA BUHTAANUN A’ZEEM.\nWhen ye heard it, why did ye not say: “It is not for us to talk of this (affair) glory be to Thee (O’ Lord)! this is a serious slander?\nيَعِظُكُمُ اللّٰهُ اَنْ تَعُوْدُوْا لِمِثْلِهٖۤ اَبَدًا اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(17)\nYAE’EZUKUMU LAAHO AN TAU’OODOOA LEMESLEH ABADAM IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN.\nGod admonisheth you that ye return not unto the like of it for ever, if ye be believers.\nوَيُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمُ الْاٰيٰتِ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(18)\nWA YOBAYYENO LAAHO LAKOMUL AL-AAAYAATE WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nAnd God maketh clear unto you the signs; and God is All Knowing, All-Wise.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُحِبُّوْنَ اَنْ تَشِيْعَ الْفَاحِشَةُ فِى الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌۙ فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ وَاَنْتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(19)\nINNAL LAZEENA YOHIBBOONA AN TASHEEA’A AL-FAAHESHATU FIL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO WA ANTUM LAA TA’LAMOON.\nVerily those who love to spread scandal about those who believe, they shall have a grievous chastisement in this world and the hereafter; and God knoweth and ye know not.\nوَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهٗ وَاَنَّ اللّٰهَ رَءُوْفٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(20)\nWA LAWLAA FAZLUL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA RAHMATOHU WA ANNAL LAAHA RA-OOFUM RAHEEM.\nHad it not been God’s grace on you and His mercy, and God is Compassionate, All-Merciful (ye would have been chastised).\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَتَّبِعُوْا خُطُوٰتِ الشَّيْطٰنِ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّتَّبِعْ خُطُوٰتِ الشَّيْطٰنِ فَاِنَّهٗ يَاْمُرُ بِالْفَحْشَآءِ وَالْمُنْكَرِ‌ ؕ وَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهٗ مَا زَكٰى مِنْكُمْ مِّنْ اَحَدٍ اَبَدًا وَّلٰكِنَّ اللّٰهَ يُزَكِّىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(21)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA TATTABE-O’O KHOTOWATIS SHAYTAANE WA MAN YYATTABEA’ KHOTOWATIS SHAYTAANE FA-INNAHU YAAMURU BIL-FAHSHAAA WAL MUNKARE WA LAWLAA FAZLUL LAAHE A’LAYKUM WA RAHMATOHU MAA ZAKAA MINKUM MIN AHADIM ABADAM WA LAAKINNA LAAHA YUZAKKEAA MAN YASHAAA-O WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nO’ ye who believe! follow ye not the steps of Satan; for whoever followeth the steps of Satan, he (the Satan) enjoineth (unto him) filth and evil; and had it not been God’s grace on you and His mercy not one of you had ever been clean, but God cleaneth whom He willeth; and God is All-Hearing, All Knowing.\nوَلَا يَاْتَلِ اُولُوا الْفَضْلِ مِنْكُمْ وَالسَّعَةِ اَنْ يُّؤْتُوْۤا اُولِى الْقُرْبٰى وَالْمَسٰكِيْنَ وَالْمُهٰجِرِيْنَ فِىْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ ‌‌ۖ  وَلْيَعْفُوْا وَلْيَصْفَحُوْا‌ ؕ اَلَا تُحِبُّوْنَ اَنْ يَّغْفِرَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(22)\nWA LAA YAATALE ULUL FAZLIL MINKUM WAALSSAA’ATE AN YYUTOOA ULIL QURBAA WAL MASAAKEENA WA MOHAAJEREENAL FEE SABEELIL LAAHE WALYAA’FOOA WALYASFAHOOA ALAA TUHEBBOONA AN YAGHFERAL LAAHO LAKUM WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nAnd let not those with bounties among you swear against giving to their kindred, to the poor, and the emigrants in the way of God, and they should pardon and turn away (overlook); What! Love ye not that God should forgive you? and God is Oft-Forgiving, All-Merciful.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَرْمُوْنَ الْمُحْصَنٰتِ الْغٰفِلٰتِ الْمُؤْمِنٰتِ لُعِنُوْا فِى الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌۙ‏(23)\nINNAL LAZEENA YARMOONA AL-MUHSANAATE AL-GHAAFELAATE MOAMENAATE LUE’ENOOA FIL DUNYAA WAL AAKHERAH WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZEEM.\nVerily they who accuse protected believer women, unaware (of the crime), shall be accursed in this world and the hereafter, and for them shall be a grievous chastisement,\nيَّوْمَ تَشْهَدُ عَلَيْهِمْ اَلْسِنَتُهُمْ وَاَيْدِيْهِمْ وَاَرْجُلُهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(24)\nYAWMA TASHHADU A’LAYHIM AALSENATUHUM WA AYDEEHIM WA ARJOLOHUM BEMAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nOn that day will bear witness against them, their tongues and their hands and their feet, as to what they did.\nيَوْمَئِذٍ يُّوَفِّيْهِمُ اللّٰهُ دِيْنَهُمُ الْحَقَّ وَيَعْلَمُوْنَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ الْحَقُّ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(25)\nYAWMA-EZIN YYOOFFEEHEMU LAAHO DEENAHUMU HAQQA WA YA’LAMOON ANNAL LAAHA HOWA HAQQO MOBEEN.\nOn that day will God mete out unto them their just due, and they will know that God, He is the Truth (Self) Evident.\nاَلْخَبِيْثٰتُ لِلْخَبِيْثِيْنَ وَالْخَبِيْثُوْنَ لِلْخَبِيْثٰتِ‌ۚ وَالطَّيِّبٰتُ لِلطَّيِّبِيْنَ وَالطَّيِّبُوْنَ لِلطَّيِّبٰتِ‌ۚ اُولٰٓئِكَ مُبَرَّءُوْنَ مِمَّا يَقُوْلُوْنَ‌ؕ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّرِزْقٌ كَرِيْمٌ‏(26)\nAALKHABEESAATU LIL-KHABEESEENA WAL KHABEESOONA LIL-KHABEESAATE WAALTTAYBAATU LELTTAYBEENA WAALTTAYBOONA LELTTAYBAATE OOLAAA-EKA MUBARRAOONA MIMMAA YAQOOLOONA LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WWAREZQUN KAREEM.\nDirty women are for the dirty men and the dirty men are for the dirty women, and the clean men are for the clean women and the good ones are for the good things; These are free from what they say; For them shall be forgiveness and sustenance honourable.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لَا تَدْخُلُوْا بُيُوْتًا غَيْرَ بُيُوْتِكُمْ حَتّٰى تَسْتَاْنِسُوْا وَتُسَلِّمُوْا عَلٰٓى اَهْلِهَا ‌ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(27)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LAA LAA BUYOOTAN GHAYRA BUYOOTEKUM HATTAA TASTAANESOOA WATUSALLEMOOA A’LAA AHLEHAA ZAA ZAALEKUM KHAYRUL LAKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TAZAKKAROON.\nO’ ye who believe! enter ye not the houses other than your (own) houses until ye have sought familiarity and saluted their inmates; This is best for you, happly ye may remember.\nفَاِنْ لَّمْ تَجِدُوْا فِيْهَاۤ اَحَدًا فَلَا تَدْخُلُوْهَا حَتّٰى يُؤْذَنَ لَكُمْ‌ۚ وَاِنْ قِيْلَ لَكُمُ ارْجِعُوْا فَارْجِعُوْا‌ۚ هُوَ اَزْكٰى لَكُمْ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ عَلِيْمٌ‏(28)\nFA-IN LAM WA LAM FEEHAA AHADAN FALAA TADKHULOOHAA HATTAA YUZANA LAKUM WA QEELA LAKOMUL ARJEU’OOA FAR-JE-O’O HOWA WA LAKUM WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOON A’LEEM.\nBut if ye find out in them any one, then enter them not until permission is given to you; and if it is said unto you ‘Get ye back’ then ye get back, for it is purer for you; and God knoweth what all ye do.\nلَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ اَنْ تَدْخُلُوْا بُيُوْتًا غَيْرَ مَسْكُوْنَةٍ فِيْهَا مَتَاعٌ لَّكُمْ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تُبْدُوْنَ وَمَا تَكْتُمُوْنَ‏(29)\nLAYSA A’LAYKUM JONAAHUN AN LAA BUYOOTAN GHAYRA MASKOONATIN FEEHAA LIL-MOTAALLAQAATE LAKUM WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO MAA TUBDOONA WA MAA TAKTOMOON.\n(There shall be) no blame on you that ye enter uninhabited houses wherein be your goods; and God knoweth what ye do openly and what ye hide.\nقُلْ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ يَغُضُّوْا مِنْ اَبْصَارِهِمْ وَيَحْفَظُوْا فُرُوْجَهُمْ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ اَزْكٰى لَهُمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا يَصْنَعُوْنَ‏(30)\nQUL LIL-MOAMENEEN YAGHUZZOOA MIN ABSAAREHIM WAYAHFAZOOA FOROOJAHUM ZAA LEKA WA LAHUM INNAL LAAHA KHABEERUM BEMAA YASNAU’OONA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) unto the believer men that they cast down their gaze and guard their private parts; that is purer for them; Verily God is All-Aware of what (all) ye do.\nوَقُلْ لِّلْمُؤْمِنٰتِ يَغْضُضْنَ مِنْ اَبْصَارِهِنَّ وَيَحْفَظْنَ فُرُوْجَهُنَّ وَلَا يُبْدِيْنَ زِيْنَتَهُنَّ اِلَّا مَا ظَهَرَ مِنْهَا‌ وَلْيَضْرِبْنَ بِخُمُرِهِنَّ عَلٰى جُيُوْبِهِنَّ‌ وَلَا يُبْدِيْنَ زِيْنَتَهُنَّ اِلَّا لِبُعُوْلَتِهِنَّ اَوْ اٰبَآئِهِنَّ اَوْ اٰبَآءِ بُعُوْلَتِهِنَّ اَوْ اَبْنَآئِهِنَّ اَوْ اَبْنَآءِ بُعُوْلَتِهِنَّ اَوْ اِخْوَانِهِنَّ اَوْ بَنِىْۤ اِخْوَانِهِنَّ اَوْ بَنِىْۤ اَخَوٰتِهِنَّ اَوْ نِسَآئِهِنَّ اَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُهُنَّ اَوِ التّٰبِعِيْنَ غَيْرِ اُولِى الْاِرْبَةِ مِنَ الرِّجَالِ اَوِ الطِّفْلِ الَّذِيْنَ لَمْ يَظْهَرُوْا عَلٰى عَوْرٰتِ النِّسَآءِ‌ وَلَا يَضْرِبْنَ بِاَرْجُلِهِنَّ لِيُعْلَمَ مَا يُخْفِيْنَ مِنْ زِيْنَتِهِنَّ‌ ؕ وَتُوْبُوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ جَمِيْعًا اَيُّهَ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(31)\nWA QUL LLELMUMENAATE YAGHZUZNA MIN AABSAAREHENNA WAYAHFAZNA FUROOJAHUNNA WA LAA YUBDEENA ZEENATAHUNNA ILLAA MAA ZAHARAL MINHAA WALYAZREBNA BEKHUMUREHENNA A’LAA JUYOOBEHENNA WA LAA YUBDEENA ZEENATAHUNNA ILLAA LEBUU’OOLATEHENNA AW AABAAA-EHINNA AW AAABAAE BUU’OOLATEHENNA AW ABNAAA-EHINNA AW ABNAAA-E BUU’OOLATEHENNA AW IKHWAANEHINNA AW BANEE IKHWAANEHINNA AW BANEE AKHAWAATEHINNA AW NESAAA-EHINNA AW MAA MALAKAT MALAKAT AWE’ AT-TAABEE’EENA GHAIRE ULIL AL-AERBATE MENAL AR-REJAALE AWE’ AT-TEFLE LAZEENA LAM YAZHAROOA A’LAA A’AWRAATE NESAAA-E WA LAA YAZREBNA BEAARJULEHENNA LEEA’LAMA MAA YUKHFEENA MIN ZEENATEHENNA WATOOBOOA ELAL LAAHE JAMEE-A’A AYYOHAS MOAMENOONA LA-A’LLAKUM TUFLEHOON.\nAnd say unto the believing women that they cast down their gaze and guard their private parts and they display not their adornment save what is apparent of it; and to draw their veils over their bosoms, and they display not their adornment save to their husbands or their fathers, or the fathers of their husband’s, or their sons, or the sons of their husbands or their brothers, or their brother’s sons, or their sister’s sons, or their women, or those whom their right hands possess, or the male servants void of sexual stimulant, or the children who have not yet attained the carnal knowledge of women’s nakedness, and let them not strike their feet (in walking) that what they hide of their adornment gets apparent; and turn ye (repentant) unto God all of you, O’ ye believers! that ye may be successful.\nوَاَنْكِحُوا الْاَيَامٰى مِنْكُمْ وَالصّٰلِحِيْنَ مِنْ عِبَادِكُمْ وَاِمَآئِكُمْ‌ ؕ اِنْ يَّكُوْنُوْا فُقَرَآءَ يُغْنِهِمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(32)\nWAANKEHOOA AL-AAYAAMAA MINKUM WA SAALEHEEN MIN E’EBAADEKUM WAAMAAEKUM IN YYAKOONOOA FUQARAAA YUGHNEHEMU LAAHO MIN FAZLEHI WAL LAAHO WAASE-U’N A’LEEM.\nAnd marry ye those among you who are single and those who are righteous ones your male slaves and your female slaves; If they be needy, God out of His grace will make them free from want; and God is All-Bounteous, All-Knowing.\nوَلْيَسْتَعْفِفِ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَجِدُوْنَ نِكَاحًا حَتّٰى يُغْنِيَهُمُ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ‌ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ يَبْتَغُوْنَ الْكِتٰبَ مِمَّا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْ فَكَاتِبُوْهُمْ اِنْ عَلِمْتُمْ فِيْهِمْ خَيْرًا ‌‌ۖ  وَّاٰ تُوْهُمْ مِّنْ مَّالِ اللّٰهِ الَّذِىْۤ اٰتٰٮكُمْ ‌ؕ وَلَا تُكْرِهُوْا فَتَيٰتِكُمْ عَلَى الْبِغَآءِ اِنْ اَرَدْنَ تَحَصُّنًا لِّتَبْتَغُوْا عَرَضَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّكْرِهْهُّنَّ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اِكْرَاهِهِنَّ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(33)\nWALYASTAA’FEFE LAZEENA LAA YAJEDOONA NEKAAHAN HATTAA YUGHNEEHUMU LAAHO MIN FAZLEH WAL LAZEENA YABTAGHOONA KETAABA MIMMAA MALAKAT AYMAANOKUM FAKAATEBOOHUM IN A’ALEMTUM FEEHIM KHAYRAN WWAA TOOHUM MIN MMAALE LAAHE LAZEE AATAAKUM WA LAA TUKREHOOA FATAYTEKUM A’LAL AL-BEGHAAE IN AARADNA TAHASSUNAN LLETABTAGHOOA A’ARAZA HAYAATID DUNYAA WA MAN YYUKREHHHUNNA FA-INNAL LAAHA MIN BA’DE AEKRAAHEHENNA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nAnd let them be in continence, those find not means to marry until God of His grace maketh them free from want; And those who seek a deed (of liberation) from among those whom your right hands possess, give them the writing if ye know of goodness in them; and give them of the wealth of God which He hath given you; and compel not your slave girls to prostitution when they desire to be chaste in order ye may seek the casual fruitions in the life of this world; and whoever compelleth them then verily after their compulsion God is Oft-Forgiving, All-Merciful.\nوَلَقَدْ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكُمْ اٰيٰتٍ مُّبَيِّنٰتٍ وَّمَثَلًا مِّنَ الَّذِيْنَ خَلَوْا مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَمَوْعِظَةً لِّلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(34)\nWA LAQAD ANZALNAA ELAYKUM AAYAATIM MMUBAYNAATIN WWAMASALAN MENAL LAZEENA KHALAW MIN QABLEKUM WA MAW-E’ZATAL LIL-MUTTAQEEN.\nAnd indeed sent We down unto you signs descriptive and an instance from those who have passed away before you, and an admonition unto the pious ones.\nاَللّٰهُ نُوْرُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ ‌ؕ مَثَلُ نُوْرِهٖ كَمِشْكٰوةٍ فِيْهَا مِصْبَاحٌ‌ ؕ الْمِصْبَاحُ فِىْ زُجَاجَةٍ‌ ؕ اَلزُّجَاجَةُ كَاَنَّهَا كَوْكَبٌ دُرِّىٌّ يُّوْقَدُ مِنْ شَجَرَةٍ مُّبٰرَكَةٍ زَيْتُوْنَةٍ لَّا شَرْقِيَّةٍ وَّلَا غَرْبِيَّةٍ ۙ يَّكَادُ زَيْتُهَا يُضِىْٓءُ وَلَوْ لَمْ تَمْسَسْهُ نَارٌ‌ ؕ نُوْرٌ عَلٰى نُوْرٍ‌ ؕ يَهْدِى اللّٰهُ لِنُوْرِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ ؕ وَ يَضْرِبُ اللّٰهُ الْاَمْثَالَ لِلنَّاسِ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ ۙ‏(35)\nALLAAHO NOORU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE MASALUL NOOREH KAMESHKAAWTIN FEEHAA MESBAAHUN AL-MESBAAHU FEE ZUJAAJATIN AALZZUJAAJATU JAAANNUW KAWKABUN DURREAAAUN YYOOQADU MIN SHAJARATIN MOBAARAKATIN ZAYTOONATIN LAA SHARQEETIN WA LAA GHARBEETIN YYAKAADU ZAYTUHAA YUZEAAAAU WA LAW LAM TAMSASHU NAARUN NOORUN A’LAA NOORIN YAHDIL LAAHO LENOOREH MAN YASHAAA-O WA YAZREBU LAAHO AL-AAMSAALA LELNNAASE WAL LAAHO BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nGod is the Light of the heavens and the earth; the similitude of His Light is as a niche in which is a lamp, the lamp is in a glass; The glass is as it were a star shining bright, lit from a blessed olive tree, neither eastern nor western, the oil whereof almost gloweth forth (of itself), and (even) though fire toucheth it not; Light upon Light: God guideth unto His Light whomsoever He willeth; and God setteth forth parables for people; and God is All- Aware of all things.\nفِىْ بُيُوْتٍ اَذِنَ اللّٰهُ اَنْ تُرْفَعَ وَيُذْكَرَ فِيْهَا اسْمُهٗۙ يُسَبِّحُ لَهٗ فِيْهَا بِالْغُدُوِّ وَالْاٰصَالِۙ‏(36)\nFEE BUYOOTIN AZENA LAAHO AN TURFAA’A WAYUZKARA FEEHAA FEEHAS YOSABBEHO LAHU FEEHAA BIL-GHUDOO WAL AAASAALE.\n(That lamp is lit) In houses which God hath permitted to be exalted and His name be mentioned therein, therein declare glory unto Him in the mornings and the evenings,\nرِجَالٌ ۙ لَّا تُلْهِيْهِمْ تِجَارَةٌ وَّلَا بَيْعٌ عَنْ ذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ وَاِقَامِ الصَّلٰوةِ وَ اِيْتَآءِ الزَّكٰوةِ‌ ۙ يَخَافُوْنَ يَوْمًا تَتَقَلَّبُ فِيْهِ الْقُلُوْبُ وَالْاَبْصَارُ ۙ‏(37)\nREJAALUN LAA TULHEEHEM TEJAARATUN WA LAA BAY-U’N A’N ELAA LAAHE WAAQAAME AS-SALAAWTE WA AEETAAE AZ-ZAKAAWTE YAKHAAFOONA YAWMAN TATAQALLABU FEEHE BALAGHATIL WA IZ ZAAGHATIL.\nMen whom neither merchandise nor any sale diverteth from the remembrance of God and constancy in prayer and paying the poor-rate; They fear the day when the hearts and eyes shall writhe of the anguish,\nلِيَجْزِيَهُمُ اللّٰهُ اَحْسَنَ مَا عَمِلُوْا وَيَزِيْدَهُمْ مِّنْ فَضْلِهٖ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَرْزُقُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ‏(38)\nLEEJZEEHUMU LAAHO AHSANAL MAA A’MELOO WAYAZEEDAHUM MIN FAZLEH WAL LAAHO YARZOQO MAN YASHAAA-O BEGHAYRIL HESAAB.\nThat God may give them the best recompense for what they have done and increase for them, out of His grace; And God provideth sustenance for whomsoever He willeth without measure.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَعْمَالُهُمْ كَسَرَابٍۢ بِقِيْعَةٍ يَّحْسَبُهُ الظَّمْاٰنُ مَآءً ؕ حَتّٰۤى اِذَا جَآءَهٗ لَمْ يَجِدْهُ شَيْئًا وَّ وَجَدَ اللّٰهَ عِنْدَهٗ فَوَفّٰٮهُ حِسَابَهٗ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَرِيْعُ الْحِسَابِ ۙ‏(39)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO A-A’MAALOHUM KASARAABIN BEQEEA’ATIN YYAHSABUHU AZ-ZAMAAANU MAAA-AN HATTAA EZAA JAAA-AHU LAM YAJEDHU SHAY-ANW WA WAJADA LAAHA I’NDAHU FAWAFFAAHU HESAABAH WAL LAAHO SAREE-U’L HESAAB.\nAs for those who disbelieve, their deeds are as a mirage in a desert, the thirsty supposeth it to be water; until he cometh unto it and findeth it naught, and findeth God with him, so he payeth unto Him his account; And God is quick in reckoning,\nاَوْ كَظُلُمٰتٍ فِىْ بَحْرٍ لُّجِّىٍّ يَّغْشٰٮهُ مَوْجٌ مِّنْ فَوْقِهٖ مَوْجٌ مِّنْ فَوْقِهٖ سَحَابٌ‌ؕ ظُلُمٰتٌۢ بَعْضُهَا فَوْقَ بَعْضٍؕ اِذَاۤ اَخْرَجَ يَدَهٗ لَمْ يَكَدْ يَرٰٮهَا‌ؕ وَمَنْ لَّمْ يَجْعَلِ اللّٰهُ لَهٗ نُوْرًا فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ نُّوْرٍ‏(40)\nAW KA-ZOLOMAATIL FEE BAHRIN LLUJJEAAAIN YYAGHSHAAHU MAWJUN MIN FAWQEH MAWJUN MIN FAWQEH SAHAABUN ZOLOMAATUNW BAA’ZUHAA FAWQA BA’Z WA EZAA AKHRAJAL YADAH LAM YAKAD YARAAHAA WA MAN LAM YAJA’ALE LAAHO LAHU NOORAN FAMAA LAHU MIN NNOORIN.\nOr like unto utter darkness in the deep sea: there covereth it a wave above another wave, above it is cloud; (with layers of) darkness one over the other; when he holdeth out his hand, he almost seeth it not; unto whomsoever God giveth not light, there is not for him any thing of light.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يُسَبِّحُ لَهٗ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَالطَّيْرُ صٰٓفّٰتٍ‌ؕ كُلٌّ قَدْ عَلِمَ صَلَاتَهٗ وَتَسْبِيْحَهٗ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِمَا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(41)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA YOSABBEHO LAHU MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WAALTTAYRU SAAAFFAATIN KULLUL QAD A’LEMA SALAATAH WATASBEEHAH WAL LAAHO A’LEEM BEMAA YAF-A’LOON.\nSeest thou not that God, He it is unto Him do glorify whoever is in the heavens and the earth? - The (very) birds with their wings spread; Each one knoweth its own (mode of) prayer and praise; And God knoweth all that they do.\nوَلِلّٰهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ۚ وَاِلَى اللّٰهِ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(42)\nLILLAAHE MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA ELAL LAAHE MASEER.\nGod’s is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth, and unto God is the ultimate return.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يُزْجِىْ سَحَابًا ثُمَّ يُؤَلِّفُ بَيْنَهٗ ثُمَّ يَجْعَلُهٗ رُكَامًا فَتَرَى الْوَدْقَ يَخْرُجُ مِنْ خِلٰلِهٖ‌ۚ وَيُنَزِّلُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مِنْ جِبَالٍ فِيْهَا مِنْۢ بَرَدٍ فَيُصِيْبُ بِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَ يَصْرِفُهٗ عَنْ مَّنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ ؕ يَكَادُ سَنَا بَرْقِهٖ يَذْهَبُ بِالْاَبْصَارِؕ‏(43)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA YUZJEAA SAHAABAN SUMMA YUALLEFU BAYNAH SUMMA YAJA’ALUH RUKAAMAN FATARAL WADQA YAKHROJO MIN KHELAALEH WAYUNAZZELU MENAL SAMAAA-E MIN JEBAALIN FEEHAA MIN BARADIN FAYUSEEBU BEHI MAN YASHAAA-O WA YASREFUH A’N MAN YASHAAA-O YAKAADUL SANAA BARQEH YAZHABU BIL-AABSAARE.\nSeest thou not that God driveth gently the clouds then joineth them together, then pileth them up (layers over layers) then seest thou the rain coming forth from their midst? He sendeth down from the heavens from the (clouds like) mountains therein of hail, afflicting with it whom He willeth and turning it away from whom He willeth; the flash of His lightning well nigh taketh away the sight.\nيُقَلِّبُ اللّٰهُ الَّيْلَ وَالنَّهَارَ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَعِبْرَةً لِّاُولِى الْاَبْصَارِ‏(44)\nYUQALLEBU LAAHO LAYLA WAN NAHAARA INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAE’EBRATAN LEAOOLEAA ULIL ABSAAR.\nGod turneth over the day and the night; verily there is a lesson for those with sight.\nوَاللّٰهُ خَلَقَ كُلَّ دَآبَّةٍ مِّنْ مَّآءٍ ‌ۚفَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّمْشِىْ عَلٰى بَطْنِهٖ‌ۚ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّمْشِىْ عَلٰى رِجْلَيْنِ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ يَّمْشِىْ عَلٰٓى اَرْبَعٍ‌ؕ يَخْلُقُ اللّٰهُ مَا يَشَآءُ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(45)\nWAL LAAHO KHALAQAL KULLA DAAAB-BATIL MIN MAAA-IN FA-MINHUM MAN YAMSHEE A’LAA BATNEH WA MINHUM MAN YAMSHEE A’LAA REJLAYNE WA MINHUM MAN YAMSHEE A’LAA AARBAA’IN YAKHLOQO LAAHO MAA YASHAAU INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nAnd God hath created every animal, of water; and of them is he who walketh upon its belly; and of them is he who walketh upon two feet; and of them is that walketh upon four (feet); Createth God whatever He willeth; Verily God over all things hath power.\nلَقَدْ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اٰيٰتٍ مُّبَيِّنٰتٍ‌ؕ وَ اللّٰهُ يَهْدِىْ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(46)\nLAQAD ANZALNAA AAYAATIM MMUBAYNAATIN WA LAAHO YAHDEE MAN YASHAAA-O ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nIndeed We have sent down signs explanatory; and God guideth whomsoever He willeth unto the right way.\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ وَبِالرَّسُوْلِ وَاَطَعْنَا ثُمَّ يَتَوَلّٰى فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ ذٰلِكَ‌ؕ وَمَاۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ بِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(47)\nWA YAQOOLOONA AAMANNAA BIL-LAAHE WABEALRRASOOLE WA ATA’NAA SUMMA YATAWALLAA FAREEQUM MINHUM MIN BA’DE ZAALEK WA MAA OOLAAA-EKA BIL-MOAMENEENA.\nAnd say they: “Believe we in God and in the Apostle and we obey; then did turn back a party of them thereafter; and these are not believers\nوَاِذَا دُعُوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ لِيَحْكُمَ بَيْنَهُمْ اِذَا فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْهُمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَ‏(48)\nWA EZAA WA ELAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI LE-YAHKOMA BAYNAHUM EZAA FAREEQUM MINHUM MO’REZOON.\nAnd when they are summoned unto God and His Apostle that he may judge between them, lo! a faction of them turn aside.\nوَاِنْ يَّكُنْ لَّهُمُ الْحَقُّ يَاْتُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ مُذْعِنِيْنَؕ‏(49)\nWA YYAKUN LAHOMUB HAQQO YAATOOA ELAYHE MUZE’ENEENA.\nAnd if right be on their side they come quickly unto Him submissive and obedient.\nاَفِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ مَّرَضٌ اَمِ ارْتَابُوْۤا اَمْ يَخَافُوْنَ اَنْ يَّحِيْفَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ‌ؕ بَلْ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(50)\nAAFEAA QOLOOBEHIM MARAZUN AMIL ARTAABOOA AM YAKHAAFOONA AN YYAHEEFA LAAHO A’LAYHIM WARASOOLUH BAL OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL ZAALEMOON.\nIs in their heart any disease or do they doubt, or fear they lest will unjustly deal with them God and His apostle; Nay! they themselves are the unjust ones.\nاِنَّمَا كَانَ قَوْلَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ اِذَا دُعُوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ لِيَحْكُمَ بَيْنَهُمْ اَنْ يَّقُوْلُوْا سَمِعْنَا وَاَطَعْنَا‌ؕ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(51)\nINNAMAA KAANA QAWLA MOAMENEEN EZAA WA ELAL LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI LE-YAHKOMA BAYNAHUM AN YAQOOLOO SAMEA’NAA WAATAA’NAA WA OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nThe answer of the believers, when they are summoned unto God and His apostle that He may judge between them, that they say: “we hear and we obey; and these it is that are the successful (ones).\nوَمَنْ يُّطِعِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَيَخْشَ اللّٰهَ وَيَتَّقْهِ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْفَآئِزُوْنَ‏(52)\nWA MAN YOTE-I’L LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WAYAKHSHA LAAHA WAYATTAQHE FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL FAAA-EZOON.\nAnd whoever obeyeth God and His apostle, and feareth God, and keepeth duty (unto) Him, these! they are the achievers.\nوَاَقْسَمُوْا بِاللّٰهِ جَهْدَ اَيْمَانِهِمْ لَئِنْ اَمَرْتَهُمْ لَيَخْرُجُنَّ‌ ۚ قُلْ لَّا تُقْسِمُوْا‌ ۚ طَاعَةٌ مَّعْرُوْفَةٌ‌  ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(53)\nWAAQSAMOOA BIL-LAAHE JAHDA AAYMAANEHEM LAIL AAMARTAHUM LAYAKHRUJUNNA QUL LAA TUQSEMOOA TAAA’ATUN MMAA’ROOFATUN INNAL LAAHA KHABEERUM BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nSwear they by God with the most solemn of their oaths that if thou doth command them they would certainly go forth; Say thou: “Swear ye not: (better than this) is obedience; verily God is well aware of whatever ye do.\nقُلْ اَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوا الرَّسُوْلَ‌ۚ فَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاِنَّمَا عَلَيْهِ مَا حُمِّلَ وَعَلَيْكُمْ مَّا حُمِّلْتُمْ‌ؕ وَاِنْ تُطِيْعُوْهُ تَهْتَدُوْا‌ؕ وَمَا عَلَى الرَّسُوْلِ اِلَّا الْبَلٰغُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(54)\nQUL AATEEU’OOA LAAHA WAATEEU’OOA YATTABE-U’R FA-IN TAWALLAW FA-INNAMAA A’LAYHE MAA HUMMELA WA A’LAYKUM MAA HUMMELTUM WA TUTEEU’OOHU TAHTADOOA WA MAA A’LAL RASOOLE ILLAA BALAAGHUL MOBEEN.\nSay thou: “Obey God and obey the Apostle, and if ye turn back, then on him is what is imposed (on him) and on you is what is imposed on you; and if ye obey him ye are guided aright; and nothing is on the Apostle save the clear conveyance (of the Message)\nوَعَدَ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مِنْكُمْ وَ عَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَيَسْتَخْلِفَنَّهُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ كَمَا اسْتَخْلَفَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ وَلَيُمَكِّنَنَّ لَهُمْ دِيْنَهُمُ الَّذِى ارْتَضٰى لَهُمْ وَلَيُبَدِّلَنَّهُمْ مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ خَوْفِهِمْ اَمْنًا‌ ؕ يَعْبُدُوْنَنِىْ لَا يُشْرِكُوْنَ بِىْ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ وَمَنْ كَفَرَ بَعْدَ ذٰ لِكَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْفٰسِقُوْنَ‏(55)\nWA-A’DAR LAAHO LAZEENA AAMANOO MINKUM WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LAYASTAKHLEFANNAHUM FIL ARZE KAMAA ASTAKHLAFA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM WALAYUMAKKENANNA LAHUM DEENAHUMU LAZIS ARTAZAA LAHUM WALAYUBADDELANNAHUM MIN BA’DE KHAWFEHEM AAMNAN YAA’BUDOONANEAA LAA YUSHREKOON BEE SHAY-ANW WA MAN KAFARA BA’DA ZAA LEKA FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL FAASEQOON.\nGod hath promised unto those of you who believe and do good deeds that He will certainly appoint them successors in the earth as He appointed successors those before them, and that certainly He shall establish for them their religion (Islam) which He hath chosen for them, and that certainly He will, after their fear, in exchange give them security; They shall worship Me; and associating not with Me aught; and whosoever disbelieveth after this, these! they are the wicked ones.\nوَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَ اٰ تُوا الزَّكٰوةَ وَاَطِيْعُوا الرَّسُوْلَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَ‏(56)\nWA AQEEMUS SALAATA WA AAA TOOA ZAKAATA WAATEEU’OOA YATTABE-U’R LA-A’LLAKUM TURHAMOON.\nAnd establish ye prayer and pay ye the poor-rate and obey the Apostle, that ye be dealt with mercy.\nلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مُعْجِزِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ۚ وَمَاْوٰٮهُمُ النَّارُ‌ؕ وَلَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(57)\nLAA TAHSABANNA LAZEENA KAFAROO MUA’JEZEENA FIL ARZE WAMAAWAAHUMU AN-NAARU WA LABESA MASEER.\nThink not that those who disbelieve can (ever) frustrate (God's plan) on earth; Their abode is the (Hell) fire; and certainly an evil is the resort.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا لِيَسْتَاْذِنْكُمُ الَّذِيْنَ مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُكُمْ وَالَّذِيْنَ لَمْ يَبْلُغُوا الْحُلُمَ مِنْكُمْ ثَلٰثَ مَرّٰتٍ‌ؕ مِنْ قَبْلِ صَلٰوةِ الْفَجْرِ وَحِيْنَ تَضَعُوْنَ ثِيَابَكُمْ مِّنَ الظَّهِيْرَةِ وَمِنْۢ بَعْدِ صَلٰوةِ الْعِشَآءِ ‌ؕ  ثَلٰثُ عَوْرٰتٍ لَّكُمْ‌ ؕ لَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَ لَا عَلَيْهِمْ جُنَاحٌۢ بَعْدَهُنَّ‌ ؕ طَوّٰفُوْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ بَعْضُكُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ‌ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمُ الْاٰيٰتِ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(58)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO LEESTAAZENKUMU LAZEENA MALAKAT AYMAANOKUM WAL LAZEENA LAM YABLUGHOOA AL-HULUMA MINKUM SALAASA MARRAATIN MIN QABLE SALAAWTE FAJR WA TAZAU’OONA SEEABAKUM MENAL AZ-ZAHEERATE WA MIN BA’DE SALAAWTE AL-E’ESHAAE SALAASU A’AWRAATIN LAKUM LAYSA A’LAYKUM WA LAA A’LAYHIM JONAAHUN BAA’DAHUNNA TAWFOONA A’LAYKUM BA’ZOKUM A’LAA ELAA KAZAALEKA YOBAYYENUL LAAHO LAKOMUL AAYAATE WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nO’ ye who believe! let those whom your right hands possess and those of you who have not reached puberty seek permission of you three times (a day) (ere they come into your presence); before the morning prayer, and when ye lay aside your garments for the heat (at midday), and after the night prayer; These are the three times of privacy for you; It is neither for you nor for them a sin (if) after those (three times); some of you go round attendant upon the others; Thus doth God maketh clear unto you the signs; and God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nوَاِذَا بَلَغَ الْاَطْفَالُ مِنْكُمُ الْحُلُمَ فَلْيَسْتَاْذِنُوْا كَمَا اسْتَاْذَنَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ‌ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ اٰيٰتِهٖ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلِيْمٌ حَكِيْمٌ‏(59)\nWA EZAA BALAGHA AL-AATFAALU MINKOMUSH AL-HULUMA FALYASTAAZENOOA KAMAA ASTAAZANA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM KAZAALEKA YOBAYYENUL LAAHO LAKUM AAAYAATEH WAL LAAHO A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nAnd when the children among you reach puberty let them seek permission even as those (of age) before them did seek permission; Thus doth God make clear to you His signs; and God is All-Knowing, All-Wise.\nوَالْقَوَاعِدُ مِنَ النِّسَآءِ الّٰتِىْ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ نِكَاحًا فَلَيْسَ عَلَيْهِنَّ جُنَاحٌ اَنْ يَّضَعْنَ ثِيَابَهُنَّ غَيْرَ مُتَبَرِّجٰتٍ ۭ بِزِيْنَةٍ‌ ؕ وَاَنْ يَّسْتَعْفِفْنَ خَيْرٌ لَّهُنَّ‌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ سَمِيْعٌ عَلِيْمٌ‏(60)\nWAL QAWAAE’EDU MENAL NESAAA-E KHAALEKA LAA YARJOON NEKAAHAN FA-LAYSA A’LAYHINNA JONAAHUN AN YA-ZA’NA SEEABAHUNNA GHAYRA MUTABARREJAATIN BEZEENATIN WA YYASTAA’FEFNA KHAYRUL LEBAASUL WAL LAAHO SAMEE-U’N A’LEEM.\nAnd of the women past child bearing, who hope not for marriage, it is no sin on them if they put off their (outer) garments, without displaying their ornaments; Yet if they restrain themselves (even from this) it is better for them; And God is All-Hearing, All Knowing.\nلَيْسَ عَلَى الْاَعْمٰى حَرَجٌ وَّلَا عَلَى الْاَعْرَجِ حَرَجٌ وَّلَا عَلَى الْمَرِيْضِ حَرَجٌ وَّلَا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِكُمْ اَنْ تَاْكُلُوْا مِنْۢ بُيُوْتِكُمْ اَوْ بُيُوْتِ اٰبَآئِكُمْ اَوْ بُيُوْتِ اُمَّهٰتِكُمْ اَوْ بُيُوْتِ اِخْوَانِكُمْ اَوْ بُيُوْتِ اَخَوٰتِكُمْ اَوْ بُيُوْتِ اَعْمَامِكُمْ اَوْ بُيُوْتِ عَمّٰتِكُمْ اَوْ بُيُوْتِ اَخْوَالِكُمْ اَوْ بُيُوْتِ خٰلٰتِكُمْ اَوْ مَا مَلَكْتُمْ مَّفَاتِحَهٗۤ اَوْ صَدِيْقِكُمْ‌ؕ لَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ اَنْ تَاْكُلُوْا جَمِيْعًا اَوْ اَشْتَاتًا‌ ؕ فَاِذَا دَخَلْتُمْ بُيُوْتًا فَسَلِّمُوْا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِكُمْ تَحِيَّةً مِّنْ عِنْدِ اللّٰهِ مُبٰرَكَةً طَيِّبَةً‌  ؕ كَذٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللّٰهُ لَكُمُ الْاٰيٰتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(61)\nLAYSA A’LAL A-A’MAA HARAJUN WA LAA A’LAL A-A’RAJE HARAJUN WA LAA A’LAL MAREEZE HARAJUN WA LAA A’LAA ANFOSEKUM AN TAAKULOOA MIN BUYOOTEKUM AW BUYOOTE AAABAAEKUM AW BUYOOTE MINHUNNA AW BUYOOTE AEKHWAANEKUM AW BUYOOTE AAKHAWTEKUM AW BUYOOTE AAA’MAAMEKUM AW BUYOOTE A’AMMAATEKUM AW BUYOOTE AAKHWAALEKUM AW BUYOOTE KHAALAATEKUM AW MAA MALAKTUM MMAFAATEHAH AW SADEEQEKUM LAYSA A’LAYKUM JONAAHUN AN TAAKULOOA JAMEE-A’A AW ASHTAATAL FA-EZAA DAKHALTUM BUYOOTAN FASALLEMOOA A’LAA ANFOSEKUM TAHEETAN MIN I’NDIL LAAHE MUBAARAKATAN TAYBATAN KAZAALEKA YOBAYYENUL LAAHO LAKOMUL AAYAATE LA-A’LLAKUM TA’QELOON.\nNo blame is there on the blind one, nor is there any blame on the lame, nor is there any blame on the sick, nor on yourselves that ye eat from your houses, or your fathers’ houses, or your mothers’ houses, or your brothers’ houses, or your sisters’ houses, or your paternal uncles’ houses, or your paternal aunts’ houses, or your maternal uncles’ houses, or your maternal aunts’ houses, or what ye possess the keys of, or of your friends’ (house); It is no sin on you that ye eat together or separately; and when ye enter houses greet ye your people with a salutation from God, blessed (and) goodly; Thus doth God maketh clear unto you His signs, that ye may understand.\nاِنَّمَا الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ وَاِذَا كَانُوْا مَعَهٗ عَلٰٓى اَمْرٍ جَامِعٍ لَّمْ يَذْهَبُوْا حَتّٰى يَسْتَاْذِنُوْهُ‌ ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَاْذِنُوْنَكَ اُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖ‌ ۚ فَاِذَا اسْتَاْذَنُوْكَ لِبَعْضِ شَاْنِهِمْ فَاْذَنْ لِّمَنْ شِئْتَ مِنْهُمْ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمُ اللّٰهَ‌ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(62)\nINNAMAA MOAMENOONA LAZEENA AAMANOO BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI WA EZAA KAANOO MA-A’HU A’LAA AMRIN JAAMEA’IN LAM YAZHABOO HATTAA YASTAAZENOOHU INNAL LAZEENA YASTAAZENOONAKA OOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA YOAMENOONA BIL-LAAHE WA RASOOLEHI FA-EZAA ASTAAZANOOKA LEBAA’ZE SHAANEHEM FAAZAN LEMAN SHETA MINHUM WAASTAGHFER LAHOMUL LAAH INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nVerily, only those are believers who believe in God and His Apostle, and when they are with him on an affair demanding collective action, they go not away until they seek his permission; Verily those who seek thy permission are they who believe in God and His Apostle; so when they seek thy permission for some affair of theirs, give permission to whomsoever thou leases of them, and seek pardon for them from God; Verily God is Oft-Forgiving, All-Merciful.\nلَا تَجْعَلُوْا دُعَآءَ الرَّسُوْلِ بَيْنَكُمْ كَدُعَآءِ بَعْضِكُمْ بَعْضًا‌ ؕ قَدْ يَعْلَمُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ يَتَسَلَّلُوْنَ مِنْكُمْ لِوَاذًا‌ ۚ فَلْيَحْذَرِ الَّذِيْنَ يُخَالِفُوْنَ عَنْ اَمْرِهٖۤ اَنْ تُصِيْبَهُمْ فِتْنَةٌ اَوْ يُصِيْبَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَ لِيْمٌ‏(63)\nLAA TAJ-A’LOO DUA’AAA RASOOLE BAYNAKUM KA-DO-A’AA-IL BAA’ZEKUM BA’ZAN QAD YA’LAMO LAAHO LAZEENA YATASALLALOONA MINKUM LEWAAZAN FALYAHZARE LAZEENA YUKHAALEFOONA A’N AMREHI AN TOSEEBAHUM FITNATUN AW YUSEEBAHUM A’ZAABUN A’ZAABAN ALEEM.\nMake ye not the addressing of the Apostle among you like your addressing one another; indeed knoweth God those from among you who steal away from you, screening themselves; so let those beware who go against his order lest a trial afflicteth them or there befalleth unto them a painful chastisement.\nاَلَاۤ اِنَّ لِلّٰهِ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ ‌ؕ قَدْ يَعْلَمُ مَاۤ اَنْتُمْ عَلَيْهِؕ وَيَوْمَ يُرْجَعُوْنَ اِلَيْهِ فَيُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا عَمِلُوْا ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(64)\nALAA INNAL LILLAAHE MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE QAD YA’LAMO MAA ANTUM A’LAYH WA YAWMA YARJEO’ON ELAYHE FAYUNABBEUHUM BEMAA A’MELOO WAL LAAHO BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nBeware! Verily God’s is what soever is in the heavens and the earth; Knoweth He indeed your state; and on the day on which they are returned unto Him, then He will inform them of what they did; and God of everything is well Aware.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Noor (The Light)\nThere are 64 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Madinah. In the commentary of Burhan it is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever constantly recites Surah an-Noor will never, in his lifetime, see any evil from his near ones and when he dies, seventy thousand angels will accompany his body up to the grave and will pray for his forgiveness.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that it is especially good for women to recite this Surah. He (s.a.w.a.) also said that the reward for reciting this Surah is equal to ten times the number of believing men and women on the Earth. The sixth Imam (a.s.) said that keeping this Surah in one’s bed prevents wet dreams."
